he ad-hoc launcher pattern - the DEFAULT judge path still has no env. Two remedy seams, pick ONE and record the other: (a) supply DUCKBRAIN_URL to the judge/tier1 launch path (gitreins config or judge harness env), or (b) teach tests/gate.sh a third typed mode that classifies a dev host with no DuckBrain URL as a disclosed skip instead of a hard exit 2 - never by letting AUGER_CI=1 downgrade on a non-runner. Do NOT weaken the fail-closed prerequisite itself. Related but distinct: AUG-158 (judge lint arm scope divergence), AUG-197 (load-dependent timeouts), AUG-193 (single-row re-judge).", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-11-24T20:06:50Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-24T23:26:20Z", "foreman_note": "serial dispatch tick auger-foreman-2026-11-24-23-13-56 (WAVE_BUDGET=1, loadavg 30 -> 1 slot): worker glm-5.3-flash@opencode-go in wt/AUG-208 @ base 689a2fd; brief /tmp/brief-aug208-20261124-2313.txt; gitreins task AUG-208 created+started", "capability_tags": ["gitreins", "judge", "gate", "evidence"], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/auger-AUG-208", "branch": "wt/AUG-208", "sessions": ["foreman-tick-2026-11-24-23-13-56"], "type": null, "worker_summary": null, "completed_at": null, "acceptance_criteria": "AC1 REPRODUCE: `GATE_MODE_ONLY=1 bash tests/gate.sh` prints `gate mode: live` on this host, and with DUCKBRAIN_URL unset `bash tests/gate.sh` exit 2 at the live-prerequisite preflight printing the DuckBrain URL error instead of running pytest; paste both outputs verbatim.\n\nAC2 CAUSE PROVEN FROM A STORED VERDICT: `jq -r '.stages.tier1.steps[]|select(.id==\"tests\")|.data.exit_code' .gitreins/history/2026-11-23/589dd5f9/verdict.json` prints 2 while that same verdict's tier2 items all read PASS, so the tier1 red is an environment abort and not a test failure; expect the same shape for 8a7e18a2 and 36569fbe.\n\nAC3 FIX LIVE: the judge/t